<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mujahid al-Amiri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1044">1044</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mujahid al-Amiri was a freedman of the Amirid household who seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denia">Dénia</a> around 1010, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> collapsed, and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Dénia. He added the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> to his realm and in 1015–1016 led a seaborne expedition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, which was driven off. His court at Dénia patronised scholars, and his maritime state was one of the strongest of the early taifas.</p></div>
